forgeVideo({"file": "07-new-artefact.en.html-player.js", "lang": "en", "title": "A layer below the intent and a new artefact", "date": "4. 10. 2026", "pace": [4.0, 8.0, 16.0], "duration": 843.7, "events": [{"k": "card", "title": "A layer below the intent and a new artefact", "text": ["Real work, not a demo: two sessions of 4 October 2026, about five hours of work shown from 09:15 to 18:08, with a break in the middle of the day.", "This is a cut. The times are real, the lines verbatim and shortened, the documents shown as they stood that day."], "dur": 8.375}, {"k": "card", "title": "What you will see", "text": ["A new artefact handed over to Claude and returned as a proposal.", "The walkthrough of its choices, one at a time.", "Claude correcting his own proposal.", "The cut between what is wanted and how it is realised, found in the conversation.", "The command that makes the next kind of artefact."], "dur": 8.25}, {"k": "scene", "no": 1, "time": "09:15", "title": "The task", "caption": [["Now", "The principal types only the number of a thread. Claude reads the thread and says what is next: add the solution design by hand, its definition and its template. Then he asks how the principal wants it composed."], ["Why", "How an artefact is born is the principal's choice, artefact by artefact (POS.1410): found together by questions, or handed over to Claude."]], "clear": true, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "type", "text": "thr 520", "typing": 0.35000000000000003, "hold": 6.8500000000000005}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Read: projects/forge/10-intent.threads.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Read: .claude/skills/forge/states/assignment.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "THR.0520, step 3: add the solution design by hand, that is its definition (.claude/skills/forge/states/solution-design.md) and its template (templates/solution-design.md), as the trial of what step 2 prepared.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "What is already decided for step 3", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- What a solution design is and what it is made of: POS.1400 and POS.1420 (SOL items, open matters as TBC, a short head in prose).", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- The shape of every definition: seven blocks per POS.1310, the definitions of the intent and the assignment as models.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- The research research/2026-10-03-how-a-solution-design-is-built.md.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "What step 3 must still solve", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- What the head of a definition must carry so that the table of artefacts in the README can be rendered from it.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Calibration of the reviewers: the lens clarity and the critic contract speak only of the assignment today.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "None of this is written anywhere yet beyond the thread and the positions.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "First question (POS.1410): how do you want the definition and the template composed?", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Hand it over to me (recommended): the ground is largely decided and step 2 went the same way. I return a proposal of both files with a list of what I assumed and chose, and you judge decisions, not prose.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Find it together: we go through the definition block by block, by questions.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Hand over, or together?", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "hand over", "typing": 0.45, "hold": 1.9674999999999998}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "end", "dur": 1.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 2, "time": "09:19", "title": "The proposal", "caption": [["Now", "Claude comes back with a proposal of two files: the definition, how the artefact is found, and the template, what comes out of it. Below it he lists nine choices he made himself."], ["Why", "Work handed over comes back as a proposal, not as a done thing. The list of assumptions and choices lets the principal judge decisions instead of reading prose."]], "clear": false, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Read: templates/assignment.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Read: templates/intent.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Here is the proposal of both files. It is not written anywhere yet, it lives only in this conversation. The files are born only on your word.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. .claude/skills/forge/states/solution-design.md", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "… Aim. The solution design says how the things wanted are realised, as the solution stands today, and is kept current. It holds what cannot be read off the thing itself: why, against what, at what price, and how the parts fit. It restates nothing of the layer above, which it cites by ID, and copies nothing of what realises it, which it names by path. It is complete for now when every item of the layer above that is in scope is realised by a part, knowingly left unanswered, or open as a TBC, and when no TBC that blocks realisation is open; it is never finished.", "n": 10, "pre": false}, {"t": "Partner. How the design is composed is the principal's choice (CLAUDE.md, Working methods, Handing over). Either way Claude proposes the parts and the choices and the principal judges them. Claude names the few real choices and does not dress every part as one: where there was no real alternative he says so and invents none, and where a reason is not known he says it is unknown. How sure he is of a claim he says in words. What the designing shows must change in what is wanted goes to the intent first (CLAUDE.md, Working methods, Intent-first). Nothing is built here: the design specifies.", "n": 10, "pre": false}, {"t": "Map.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- what is to be realised: the items of the layer above the design answers, and what of them it knowingly leaves unanswered;", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- the ground: what already exists and is kept or replaced, what stands around it, and what the principal has fixed in advance;", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- the approach as a whole: the few ideas the solution rests on;", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- the parts: what is built or done, by whom where it is not software, and where each is realised;", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- how the parts work together, and what holds across them;", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- the choices: for each real one, what it was chosen against, doing nothing or the least that would do among it, and what it costs;", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- what is open or unproven: what would close it, and whether it blocks realisation;", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- how it will be known to hold: by what the thing is compared with the design;", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- the way there, where the solution replaces something that runs;", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- what is deliberately not designed and left to the file or to the one who realises. …", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. templates/solution-design.md", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "# <Project> — Solution design", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "## How the parts work together", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "## Parts", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- SOL.0010 <Name>. <What it is and what it answers for.> Realises: POS.NNNN, POS.NNNN. Choice: <chosen, against what, at what cost | no real alternative>. Where: <path>.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "## Across the parts", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "## Open", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "What I assumed and chose", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. The Map has ten areas; the research proposed eleven, I merged two.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. When the design is complete: my wording, POS.1420 does not say.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "3. A TBC also carries \"blocks realisation: yes/no\".", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "4. Two ways in: forward and backward (\"recovered\").", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "5. A SOL item has a fixed order with labels Realises:, Choice:, Where:.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "6. The coverage map is a tool of the pass, not part of the document.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "7. audience: whoever realises the solution in the template's header.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "8. The head of a definition for the README table: add nothing.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "9. /challenge <persona> solution-design as an instrument; unverified.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "What the proposal deliberately does not solve", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- A check that holds the design against what realises it.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- The version of the layer the design was derived from.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- The calibration of the reviewers and the iteration of the README recipe.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Do you want to judge the proposal as a whole, or go through the nine choices one by one?", "n": 2, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "end", "dur": 7.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 3, "time": "09:58", "title": "The principal's counter-thought", "caption": [["Now", "The principal questions choice 4 and wants a check that says what belongs in which artefact. Claude first agrees with a new check, then reads the critic clarity and corrects his opinion."], ["Why", "Claude does not add a mechanism the forge already has. What he does not know he first verifies on the files, and says what he verified it on."]], "clear": true, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "type", "text": "ad 4 dunno if we should bring that into the system for one case. IMO we go fix it now in the forge but otherwise dunno. but we definitely need a check that checks the artefacts and says whether they have what belongs there and proposes a move if needed ??", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "My opinion, three points, none of it written anywhere:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. Point 4: I agree, drop the backward way from the definition.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. The check is a good idea and has a model in the forge.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "3. These are two different checks, and I would not use the new one for step 4.", "n": 2, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 12.35}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "thats the question clarity can do it - im not saying it has to be new", "typing": 3.45, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "I must verify that before I answer: I will read the lens clarity and the critic contract.", "n": 2, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 1.685}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Read: .claude/agents/critic-clarity.md and the critic contract", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Yes, it can, and having read both files I think clarity is the right place. With that I correct my earlier opinion that it would be a new check. Verified on .claude/agents/critic-clarity.md and on the critic contract.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "Proposal: no new check. In step 3 I adjust the lens clarity and drop the backward way from the definition (your point 4). The area in the lens would read:", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Scope hygiene. Content that belongs to another artefact, judged by the Aim of the artefact's own definition (.claude/skills/forge/states/<artefact>.md), stated there and not here: an intent that solves, an assignment that solves or carries machinery of delivery, a solution design that restates the layer above or copies what realises it. The finding names the artefact the passage belongs to and proposes the move in full.", "n": 7, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 12.915}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "a", "typing": 0.05, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "end", "dur": 1.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 4, "time": "10:00", "title": "The choices one by one", "caption": [["Now", "Claude goes through the choices one at a time: when the design is complete, what the Map looks for, what a SOL item looks like. Each comes with its wording, a recommendation and a reason; the principal answers with one letter."], ["Why", "A list for decision is worked one item at a time. What is accepted is carried in the conversation and written once, at the end of the round."]], "clear": false, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Accepted: no new check, the boundary between artefacts is held by the lens clarity with the new wording of the area \"Scope hygiene\", the backward way leaves the definition. Carried in the conversation, not written anywhere yet.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "Next choice (points 2 and 3 of the list, they belong together): when the solution design is complete.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "POS.1420 does not say when the design is complete. But the Aim block must say it; by POS.1310 it is the one place where completion stands.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "I recommend my wording. Since it goes beyond POS.1420, the position would be amended with the same at the write (intent first).", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "It is complete for now when every item of the layer above that is in scope is realised by a part, knowingly left unanswered, or open as a TBC, and when no TBC that blocks realisation is open; it is never finished.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "a", "typing": 0.05, "hold": 6.454999999999998}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Next choice (point 1): what the Map is to look for. I recommend these ten. Reason: each has support in the research, and an empty area costs nothing, it is enough to say \"does not apply\".", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "- what is to be realised: the items of the layer above the design answers, and what of them it knowingly leaves unanswered;", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- the ground: what already exists and is kept or replaced, what stands around it, and what the principal has fixed in advance;", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- the approach as a whole: the few ideas the solution rests on;", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- the parts: what is built or done, by whom where it is not software, and where each is realised;", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- how the parts work together, and what holds across them;", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- the choices: for each real one, what it was chosen against, doing nothing or the least that would do among it, and what it costs;", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- what is open or unproven: what would close it, and whether it blocks realisation;", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- how it will be known to hold: by what the thing is compared with the design;", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- the way there, where the solution replaces something that runs;", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- what is deliberately not designed and left to the file or to the one who realises.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "a", "typing": 0.05, "hold": 6.565000000000001}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Next choice (point 5): what a SOL item looks like. I recommend labels in the text. Reason: the design is to stand against the files and against the layer above it, and both are easier to verify when the references are always in the same place.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "- A SOL is a part of the solution, or a matter that holds across parts. It says what the part is and what it answers for, then in this order: Realises: the IDs of the layer above, never their wording; Choice: what was chosen, against what, and what it costs, or that there was no real alternative; Where: the path.", "n": 5, "pre": false}, {"t": "And in the template:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- SOL.0010 <Name>. <What it is and what it answers for.> Realises: POS.NNNN, POS.NNNN. Choice: <chosen, against what, at what cost | no real alternative>. Where: <path>.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 14.415}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "a", "typing": 0.05, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "end", "dur": 1.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 5, "time": "10:18", "title": "A challenger of its own", "caption": [["Now", "The principal wants a challenger of its own for the solution design, a solution architect. Claude shows that the rule on an accepted challenge then does not fit, and rewrites it twice after the principal's remarks. The second remark is better than his own wording, and Claude says so."], ["Why", "A new layer brings only what it must: here a persona and one amended position. What is wanted does not change without a thread in which the principal decides it."]], "clear": true, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "type", "text": "IMO we need a challenger for the solution design. a solution architect who challenges it, for the brd a business analyst and so on. cto can look at everything...", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Understood, I take it as a modification, the point stays open. I have reworked the proposal after you: there will be a challenger for the solution design, a persona of its own.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "The rule \"an accepted challenge must change the intent\" stands in POS.0440, in CLAUDE.md and in the command /challenge. The architect's challenge will often change only the design. So the rule must be widened, the intent first, the other two places after it.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "An accepted challenge must change the artefact it concerns, otherwise it was not accepted; where it touches what is wanted, the intent changes first.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 13.62}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "m nothing has to, depends on the context. it should be fixed everywhere its needed. a fix in the solution design doesnt have to mean a change elsewhere. only in the case when we find in the solution design that the implementation is either so expensive or impossible that the assignment has to change", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Understood: no \"must change this document\". An accepted challenge is mended where it is needed, and a fix in the solution design sets off nothing else by itself. It goes higher only when the design shows that realisation is so expensive or impossible that the assignment must change.", "n": 5, "pre": false}, {"t": "An accepted challenge is mended wherever it needs to be, and one that mends nothing was not accepted. A challenge of a layer below the intent is mended in that layer and changes nothing above it, unless it shows that what is wanted cannot be realised or only at a price not worth paying: then what is wanted changes, the intent first (POS.0900).", "n": 6, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 12.72}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "m shouldnt a thr be born for things like this? cant a thr actually be born from any document? just an idea, something has to be finished...", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 3.05}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Yes, and I think it is better than my wording.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "When the design or a challenge shows that what you want must change, that is not a change of the intent yet. It is an undecided matter that you have still to decide, and that is exactly what a thread is for. My sentence \"the intent changes first\" skipped that step.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "A distinction I would keep: an open question about the solution stays in the design as a TBC. A thread in the intent is born only where it concerns what you want, or a thing to be finished that belongs to no artefact.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "In POS.0440, in place of today's sentence:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "An accepted challenge is mended wherever it needs to be, and one that mends nothing was not accepted. A challenge of a layer below the intent is mended in that layer and changes nothing above it, unless it shows that what is wanted cannot be realised or only at a price not worth paying: then a thread is opened in the intent, citing the challenge, and what is wanted is decided there.", "n": 6, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "end", "dur": 4.16}, {"k": "scene", "no": 6, "time": "10:50", "title": "The critic reads by the definition", "caption": [["Now", "At the calibration of the critic, the principal asks about nine questions in the critic clarity, all written for one artefact. They arrive at the critic judging by the artefact's definition, and the questions leave the critic."], ["Why", "The definition of an artefact is the measure for everyone who reads it. A critic that cannot judge by it is a finding about the definition."]], "clear": true, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "type", "text": "what are those questions? doesnt seem quite right to have questions for one specific artefact in clarity? plus we never used them :-)", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Here they are, all nine are written for the assignment:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. Is the objective stated as an outcome, and unambiguously?", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. Are the scope boundaries stated, including what is out?", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "3. Is the Requirement style kept throughout?", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "4. Are constraints separated from requirements?", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "5. Are the deliverables feasible, with owners and dates?", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "6. Does every open question have an owner?", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "7. Are success criteria present, delegated, or left out?", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "8. Is the detail assigning, not solving?", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "9. Is a Terms section present and matching what the document uses?", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 9.125}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "m IMO those questions have no business in the critic. the definition of the artefact should be so good that the critic validates it by it. if we wanted such critic questions and maybe its a good idea, they have to be in the definition of the artefact ??", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "My opinion, three points, none of it written anywhere:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. I agree, and the definition already has a place for it. Those nine questions are almost exactly what the definition of the assignment says, only rewritten as yes/no. A critic that reads the definition will therefore validate it by that. But I would rest it on the Aim block (what is to hold of the artefact at the end) and on the rules of the items, not on the Map. By POS.1320 the Map is explicitly not a list of criteria. If the critic ticked it off, it would bend it.", "n": 8, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. I would not add a new block \"questions for the critic\" to the definitions now.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "3. A side gain: it measures the quality of a definition. When the critic cannot validate by the definition, that is a finding about the definition, not about the artefact. That fits POS.1380, by which definitions are mended where the work shows a weakness.", "n": 4, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "m so we take those questions out of the clarity lens right?", "typing": 2.95, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Yes. The section \"Advisory checklist\" leaves the lens clarity whole, all nine questions. They move nowhere.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 2.245}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "a", "typing": 0.05, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "end", "dur": 1.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 7, "time": "11:06", "title": "The reader and the write", "caption": [["Now", "The last choice is who reads the design: a person, or an agent that programs from it. Then Claude lists what is carried only in the conversation, the principal says \"write\", Claude reflects back, and after \"yes\" he writes."], ["Why", "One write at the end of the round, on the principal's word. Written means a file and a section. What is only in the conversation is said to be so, out loud."]], "clear": true, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "type", "text": "m so the solution design is read either by a person who goes to implement it but codex can also read it to go program it", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Understood: the reader is whoever realises the solution, and that may be a person or an agent, Codex for example.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "audience: whoever realises the solution, a person or an agent", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "An agent has neither the conversation nor you at hand, it reads only the document. So the design must stand on its own. I propose to say it in one sentence in the Aim block:", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "It is read by whoever realises the solution, a person or an agent, without the principal in the room.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark / write", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 11.09}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "a", "typing": 0.05, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "That completes the list of choices. Everything below is carried only in the conversation and is not written anywhere yet:", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. Definition and template of the solution design, as amended.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. Lens clarity: the new \"Scope hygiene\", the checklist gone.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "3. Critic contract: calibration by the artefact's own definition.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "4. A new persona challenger-architect.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "5. POS.0440 in its new wording, with CLAUDE.md and /challenge.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "6. Threads: origin \"a document by path\", artefact tag, threads.md.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "7. POS.1420 amended with completion and blocking for a TBC.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "8. Thread THR.0520: step 3 done.", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 7.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "write", "typing": 0.25, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Read: projects/forge/10-intent.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "I reflect the whole round back. Nothing is written yet, everything below is only in the conversation. The intent goes to version 4.54 (2026-10-04), one round, one version.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "A. New files (three)", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. .claude/skills/forge/states/solution-design.md", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. templates/solution-design.md", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "3. .claude/agents/challenger-architect.md … Shall I write it like this?", "n": 3, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 1.9874999999999998}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "yes", "typing": 0.15000000000000002, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Write: .claude/skills/forge/states/solution-design.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Write: templates/solution-design.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Write: .claude/agents/challenger-architect.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Edit: projects/forge/10-intent.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Edit: projects/forge/10-intent.history.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Written", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- New files:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- .claude/skills/forge/states/solution-design.md", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- templates/solution-design.md", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- .claude/agents/challenger-architect.md", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- projects/forge/10-intent.md at 4.54: header, POS.0440, POS.0230, POS.0120, POS.1420, POS.1310.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Not yet written, only in the conversation", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- The rename of the threads file, tags on 29 threads, the update of THR.0520.", "n": 2, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 2.0175}, {"k": "end", "dur": 1.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 8, "time": "15:06", "title": "The first solution design", "caption": [["Now", "In the afternoon comes step 4: write the forge's first solution design and cut the solution out of the intent. The principal hands the work over, the result to go to tmp and through a check. At his question about POS.0120 Claude admits he left the cut half done, and proposes to finish it."], ["Why", "The intent changes first and nothing is made up: where a reason is not known, the design says so. What Claude left open he says out loud, and the principal can send it back."]], "clear": true, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "type", "text": "lets continue thr 520", "typing": 1.05, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Read: .claude/skills/forge/states/solution-design.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Step 4 of the thread THR.0520: write 40-solution-design.md of the forge project and move the solution out of the intent.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- It is a one-off move: the solution is carried over as it stands in the intent.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Where a reason can no longer be read from the intent or the history, it is written that it is unknown. Nothing is made up.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- The intent changes first: the \"how\" leaves the positions and the \"what and why\" stays.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Proposal: hand it over to me (handing over). I go through the whole intent 4.54 and return to you the sorting of every position and a proposal of the solution design v0.1 with a list of what I assumed and what I chose.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 13.159999999999997}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "m lets do it like with the history. work it out on documents and save them to tmp. then we run a check over it sort out the findings and accept", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 4.05}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Read: projects/forge/10-intent.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Write: tmp/solution-design/40-solution-design.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Write: tmp/solution-design/ops.txt", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Write: tmp/solution-design/notes.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "What is in tmp/solution-design/", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- 40-solution-design.md: proposal of the solution design v0.1, 30 SOL items, 2 TBC", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- ops.txt: the list of cuts, what leaves which position and into which SOL", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- notes.md: the rules of the sorting, what I chose, what is in doubt", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "Scope of the cut", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- 26 positions are shortened: the mechanism leaves, what you want and why stays.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- 5 positions leave whole and their IDs end.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "What I chose and you may decide otherwise", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. Five positions leave whole.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. Five positions are rewritten whole, because wish and mechanism were interwoven sentence by sentence.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "3. The references to files in the positions stayed (about sixty). They rightly belong in SOL, but that would change a sentence in POS.0120, that is a stance, and that is yours.", "n": 3, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 10.82}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "whats pos 120 that because of it we dont do 60 places right?", "typing": 3.0, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "POS.0120 is the position on what the intent is and what one position may carry. It says a position is to name the file that carries it out.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "You are right that it is half done. After step 4 the intent will still carry sixty paths to files and POS.0120 will describe a rule that the solution design replaced.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "Proposal: do it all now.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. The paragraph in POS.0120 changes: a position says what is to be achieved and why; what carries it out is named by the solution design, where the project has one.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. The references to files leave the positions for the Where of the SOLs concerned, with Was in the history like everything else.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "3. The same sentence also stands in the definition of the intent, so that is amended too.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 14.04}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "a", "typing": 0.05, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "end", "dur": 1.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 9, "time": "15:32", "title": "Does the design stand on its own?", "caption": [["Now", "The principal asks whether the forge can be built from the solution design alone. Claude answers that by the definition it cannot, and asks what exactly must be possible. The principal's answer exposes a fault in how the solution design was defined the day before."], ["Why", "The cut between what is wanted and how it is realised is not given in advance. It is found in the conversation, and Claude names the fault as a fault."]], "clear": true, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "type", "text": "does the solution design in our definition stand on its own (so the solution design is enough for me to build it) or do i need the intent (assignment, brd...) and the solution design to build it? in theory the forge should be buildable from the solution design alone", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "By our definition it does not stand on its own. To build you need the solution design and the layer above it, and for the forge today a third thing as well: the engine's files themselves, because the detail of the commands, templates and scripts is not in the design, only the path to them.", "n": 5, "pre": false}, {"t": "Is it to be possible to build the forge from the solution design from scratch, without today's files (on another tool, say), or is it enough that the forge can be further built and mended from it with the files at hand, only without reading the intent?", "n": 4, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "im fine with needing the intent too for the solution design. but to build the forge surely i cant need the forge documents. you have to build them from it right?", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 6.925}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "You are right, and it is a fault in how we built the solution design on 2026-10-03. The forge's files are the product. The instructions the product is built by cannot point to it for the detail.", "n": 4, "pre": false}, {"t": "The sentence in POS.1420 would read roughly like this:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "An item says of its part everything needed to build it: what it does, what it takes and gives, the rules it keeps and the steps where their order is a decision. The file that realises a part is its product, named in Where, and never the owner of its detail: the forge must be buildable from the intent and the solution design alone. The design specifies and does not copy: the wording of a file is the file's.", "n": 7, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 13.23}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "the goal should be that i take the forge artefacts throw them into codex and it builds me the forge (ideal scenario of course but thats the idea). question is whether to force the forge over the knee but for new projects it has to be that way!!!", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Proposal: do not force the forge over the knee, but do not exempt it either. Do it in parts and mark it honestly.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- The rule changes now and holds for the forge too.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- The forge's solution design is written by the new rule, but not all at once. Every SOL item says in plain words where it stands.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Right now I do two parts in full as a trial, one of scripts and one of skills.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 9.02}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "m for me we have to change the pos so it holds like this in other cases. with the forge - there is some history of how it came about and its specific in that the forge makes itself (in the future i will send it to codex or send it to the team to do it and it has to hold. i agree, lets do it somehow partially. i agree with the two examples. is everything clear? ask if needed", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Almost everything is clear. I have one question.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "When Codex or the team builds it, is it to be the same forge for Claude Code (the same skills, agents, hooks, only written anew), or a forge for their tool that does the same by other means?", "n": 3, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 12.200000000000001}, {"k": "end", "dur": 1.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 10, "time": "15:41", "title": "Architecture and specification", "caption": [["Now", "The principal tells the solution architecture apart from a technical specification. Claude withdraws his proposal: the solution design stays the architecture, the principle is written into the intent, and a technical specification layer is not introduced yet. The principal wants the principle written at once, and Claude writes intent 4.55."], ["Why", "The chain grows by adding a layer, not by inflating one that exists. A decided matter is written into the intent, and the write names the file and the section."]], "clear": false, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "type", "text": "IMO thats already the difference between solution architecture and technical analysis. in solution its general in technical theres the detail too. are we to introduce a technical specification too? isnt this growing too much? dunno", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "The difference is real and you have it right: the solution architecture says what the thing is made of and why, a technical specification says the detail it is built by.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "Is it growing too much? Yes, if we cram it into the solution design. The last proposal, that every SOL item carry everything needed to build, would make one document of both. I withdraw it.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "Proposal: write the principle now, do not add the layer.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. The solution design stays the architecture, as POS.1420 describes it today.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. The principle you care about goes into the intent: from the artefacts of the chain the thing must be buildable without a look at the finished product.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "3. A technical specification as a layer is not introduced now. It is written into THR.0520 among the open matters. The chain is built for this: a layer is one definition more.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "4. The two examples are not written, and step 4 continues with the check.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Why not now: in the forge the product is text for a model. A skill's specification would be almost a copy of it, and two almost equal versions of fifty files are exactly what POS.1070 stands against.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "a", "typing": 0.05, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Edit: tmp/solution-design/ops.txt", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "The wording to be added at the end of POS.1400:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "From the artefacts of the chain the thing must be buildable without a look at the finished product: the product is what is built, never a source of its own design. How deep the chain must go for that is the project's: the solution design gives the architecture, a technical specification the detail where the one who builds needs it. Present shape 2026-10-04.", "n": 6, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 8.05}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "m shouldnt we write 1400 straight into the intent? im not going to decide it its already decided", "typing": 3.5, "hold": 0.8}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Yes, it can be done. Writing now means one version more: POS.1400 as 4.55, the move of the solution then as 4.56. … (a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 4, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 2.37}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "a", "typing": 0.05, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Edit: projects/forge/10-intent.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Edit: projects/forge/10-intent.history.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Written as intent 4.55. It is not saved to git.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- projects/forge/10-intent.md, POS.1400: a new end of the position with the principle, dated \"Present shape 2026-10-04\". Header: version 4.55.", "n": 3, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 2.0575}, {"k": "end", "dur": 1.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 11, "time": "16:00", "title": "An isolated check of the first design", "caption": [["Now", "An isolated agent that never saw the conversation compared the old and the new intent with the solution design and found 19 findings. One high finding is exactly the fault the definition warns against: alternatives Claude made up. Claude accepts the finding, and after the save at 17:29 he reminds the principal that he has not read the design whole."], ["Why", "The first artefact of a new kind is itself a proposal. A check that does not know the conversation reads it, and the principal judges it."]], "clear": true, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "tool", "text": "Write: tmp/solution-design/report.md", "line": 0.22}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "The check's report is on disk: tmp/solution-design/report.md, 19 findings (2 high, 9 medium, 8 low).", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "What the check did not find: no lost text of the intent, no citation of a departed position, no non-existent path in Where.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "V.02, high: three alternatives in the Choice field I made up", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "SOL.0120: dispatcher \"against one command per verb or per artefact\"; the intent says only \"never by verb\" (POS.0580) SOL.0420: two commands \"against one that always runs the model\"; the intent says only that they are divided by cost (POS.0590) SOL.0210: Markdown tables \"against a store a program reads\"; the intent says nothing", "n": 6, "pre": false}, {"t": "The finding is justified, and it is exactly the fault the definition warns against: where a reason is not known, it is to be said that it is not known.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "Proposal: accept the verifier's wording.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "SOL.0120: a dispatcher with state files against one command per verb; what else it was chosen against is not recorded. SOL.0420: two commands divided by cost; what they were chosen against is not recorded. SOL.0210: Markdown tables; what they were chosen against and why is not recorded in the intent.", "n": 6, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "a", "typing": 0.05, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "State after the save", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- Solution design 0.1 is a proposal you have not read whole.", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 2.377499999999999}, {"k": "end", "dur": 1.0}, {"k": "scene", "no": 12, "time": "17:32", "title": "The command for a new kind", "caption": [["Now", "Step 5 is a command that adds a new kind of artefact. From adding the solution design by hand Claude derives six outputs and proposes the command's name. At the principal's questions he admits twice that his reason was weaker than he made it."], ["Why", "A kind of artefact is two files, the definition and the template, and around them only what must know them. The command decides nothing: it leads by a map, and each output is born on the principal's word."]], "clear": true, "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "type", "text": "lets continue with step 5", "typing": 1.25, "hold": 8.0}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Step 3, the solution design added by hand, showed what adding one really costs today: the definition in states/, the template in templates/, besides that the challenger persona architect, an adjustment of the critic's calibration and of the lens clarity. And in the intent the positions that say what the artefact is.", "n": 5, "pre": false}, {"t": "For the first time by the new order: first into the intent, what you want the user to be able to do. Then into the solution design, how the command does it. Only then the command's file.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "I propose the command lead to the same six outputs, in this order:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "1. A position in the forge intent: what the artefact is, for whom, and why.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "2. The definition in states/<name>.md, seven blocks per POS.1310.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "3. The template in templates/<name>.md, paired with the definition.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "4. ID prefixes, if the artefact needs its own.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "5. Reviewers: a challenger of its own, and what the critic must not report as a defect.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "6. An item in the forge's solution design: where it is realised.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "The command itself decides none of this. Each of the six outputs is born on your word.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 16.0}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "a", "typing": 0.05, "hold": 2.919999999999998}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Proposal: option 1, /new-artefact <name>.", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 0.6}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "explain more option 1 and why you decided as you did pros cons", "typing": 3.1, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "It is about what the definition of a new kind of artefact is written from, that is the file states/<name>.md with its seven blocks.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Option A: no skeleton (that is what I chose) Option B: a skeleton templates/definition.md", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "That reason is weaker than I made it. In the Partner I myself wrote the rule \"never copy a definition\", and option A leads straight to copying.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "Proposal: change the choice to B.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 6.202500000000001}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "m why is the template for artefacts called definition?", "typing": 2.7, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Because it is not a template of an artefact. It is the skeleton of the other file of the pair, and that one is called \"definition\" in the forge.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "Every kind of artefact has two files:", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "- .claude/skills/forge/states/<name>.md: how the artefact is found, seven blocks, map, course. The forge calls it definition.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "- templates/<name>.md: what is to come out, header, sections, shape of an item. The forge calls it template.", "n": 2, "pre": false}, {"t": "Proposal: templates/artefact-definition.md.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 6.077500000000001}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "why dont we want to rename it all at once so its done??", "typing": 2.75, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "say", "paras": [{"t": "Because I estimated the cost without counting it, and I estimated it wrong. Now I have counted it, and it is a small thing that can be done at once: 3 files to rename, 14 citations in 8 live files.", "n": 3, "pre": false}, {"t": "Proposal: rename now, in this round.", "n": 1, "pre": false}, {"t": "(a)ccept / (m)odify / (q)uestion / (r)eject / (p)ark", "n": 1, "pre": false}], "line": 0.22, "hold": 5.335}, {"k": "hold", "dur": 0.2}, {"k": "type", "text": "a", "typing": 0.05, "hold": 0.35}, {"k": "think", "dur": 0.8}, {"k": "end", "dur": 1.0}, {"k": "card", "title": "What to take away", "text": ["A kind of artefact is two files: its definition, how it is found, and its template, what comes out of it.", "A new layer is added, not patched in: its own two files, and around it only what must know it: a position in the intent, a reviewer, a prefix, a command.", "The intent says what is wanted and why, the layer below how it is realised. Where the design shows that what is wanted must change, it goes up as a thread and the intent changes first.", "The first of a kind is itself a proposal: Claude lists what he assumed and chose, an isolated check reads it, the principal judges it."], "dur": 16.125}]});
